course: dictionary
lesson: 164
title: Agaric: a mushroom word in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An agaric is a mushroom with a cap on top and gills underneath. The words around a new word give you clues. In «The red toadstool with white spots, the fly agaric, is poisonous», the words after the comma tell you that the fly agaric is the red toadstool with white spots.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you guess. «The death cap, which looks plain and harmless, can kill» shows that a mushroom can look safe and still be dangerous. The clue is the word «harmless», which is followed by «can kill».
explain: Safety comes first. «Nobody should ever eat a wild mushroom unless an expert has checked it.» Context can help you understand a word, but you must never pick or eat a wild mushroom just because it looks like a picture in a book.
fact: An agaric is a mushroom with a cap and gills underneath.
fact: Gills are thin plates under the cap, and they release spores.
fact: «Fly agaric» means the red mushroom with white spots, which is poisonous.
fact: The fly agaric grows in birch and pine woods, as the sentence «grows in birch and pine woods» shows.
fact: The white spots on a fly agaric are bits of the skin that wrapped the young mushroom, and they can wash off in the rain.
exercise: «The red toadstool with white spots, the fly agaric, is poisonous.» What is a fly agaric? | *A red mushroom with white spots, which is poisonous | A blue flower that grows in gardens | A kind of bird with spots
exercise: Why should nobody eat a wild mushroom unless an expert has checked it? | *Some mushrooms look harmless but are poisonous | Wild mushrooms are always too big to eat | Experts only like the taste | Mushrooms cannot be seen in woods
exercise: The fly agaric has white spots that can wash off in the rain. Why are the spots there? | They make the mushroom grow faster | They show that it is safe to eat | They are paint from a cartoon | *They are bits of the skin that wrapped the young mushroom
test: What is a gill on an agaric? | A kind of root | A stalk that grows in the ground | A white spot on the skin | *A thin plate under the cap that releases spores
test: Which mushroom is red with white spots and poisonous? | Death cap | Blue bell flower | *Fly agaric
exam: Jayden says all agarics are poisonous. What is the best reply? | *No, agaric means any mushroom with a cap and gills, and the fly agaric is one poisonous example | Yes, every mushroom is poisonous | No, agaric means a bird with spots
